Fix the tail -F message for a new or replaced file.
When a followed name appears or is replaced, tail said "following end
of new file" but reads the new file from its start, as it should since
all of its contents are new. Say "following new file", as GNU tail
does.

---
 coreutils/tail.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/coreutils/tail.c
+++ b/coreutils/tail.c
@@ -370,7 +370,7 @@
 					/* Looks like file has been created/renamed/deleted */
 					new_fd = open(filename, O_RDONLY);
 					if (new_fd >= 0) {
-						bb_error_msg("%s has %s; following end of new file",
+						bb_error_msg("%s has %s; following new file",
 							filename, (fd < 0) ? "appeared" : "been replaced"
 						);
 						if (fd < 0) {
